  "tibetan_transliteration": "\u0f58\u0f51\u0f7c\u0f0b\u0f66\u0fa1\u0f7a\u0f0b\u0f62\u0f92\u0fb1\u0f53\u0f0b\u0f42\u0fb1\u0f72\u0f0b\u0f51\u0f7c\u0f53\u0f0b\u0f56\u0f66\u0fa1\u0f74\u0f66",
  "comments": "This work is a concise guide on the Mah\u0101y\u0101nas\u016btr\u0101la\u1e45k\u0101ra (ID:3746) (ascribed by the author to Maitreya in the conclusive verses), with references to Vasubandhu\u2019s Vy\u0101khya/Bh\u0101\u1e63ya (ID:5571). The Tibetan version of these source-texts, the first of which is the most frequently cited, sometimes differs from the canonical translation. Both texts in the canon were translated by \u015a\u0101kyasi\u1e43ha and Bande dpal brtsegs; the first was revised by rNgog Blo ldan shes rab, together with Parahitabhadra and Sajjana. The differences pertaining the Vy\u0101khya might represent a revision of its translation by rNgog Blo ldan shes rab that did not find its way into the canon.\r\nThis work probably corresponds to the \"don bdus\" listed by several Tibetan scholars (see <<Kano 2016 [BAQ9MH4T]>>: 203). A \"rnam bshad\" is also listed, which is not extant (ID: 6052).",
  "alternative_names": "mdo sde'i rgyan don bsdus\r\nmdo sde'i rgyan gyi don bsdus\r\nmdo sde rgyan gyi don bsdus",
